{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310741,"nonce":"XQmn5DUoGCnxSFZYUKUrSDOBvGU=","title":"`var b;` — an untyped local declared without an initializer and assigned in later branches — reads GARBAGE. `var b:Int = 0;` fixes it ...","message":"Inside a loop, this reads garbage:\n\n```haxe\nvar c = unsafeCodeAt(s, i);\nvar b;                      // \u003c- untyped, no initializer\nif (c == '+'.code) { b = ' '.code; i++; }\nelse if (...)      { b = (h1 \u003c\u003c 4) | h2; i += 3; }\nelse               { b = c; i++; }\n// ... uses b\n```\n\nObserved while writing `StringTools.urlDecode`: `urlDecode(\"a%20b\")` returned\n`` `P@ `` and every ASCII round-trip failed. Changing the declaration to\n`var b:Int = 0;` made all 29 oracle cases and a 136-input round-trip match Haxe\n4.3.6 exactly, with no other edit.\n\nSo the defect is the untyped deferred-initialization local, not the surrounding\nlogic. Not minimised further — worth a proper repro and root-cause. Suspect the\nsame family as [[bugs-bitwise-infer-dynamic-boxes-reassign]] (fixed 013aad05,\n`RAYZOR_ASSIGN_DEBUG=1`), where an inferred local reassigned in branches boxed\nas Dynamic.\n\n**Write `var x:T = \u003cinit\u003e;` in haxe-std rather than `var x;`.** The failure is\nloud enough to catch when the output is checked against the oracle, and silent\nif it is not.\n\n\nThe first version of that decoder used a `rayzor.Bytes` buffer. It was CORRECT\nby both oracle suites, but adding that dependency to `StringTools.hx` perturbed\nstdlib compile order and broke `haxe.Int64` field registration:\n`Issue11475, Issue11888, Issue2752, Issue3203, Issue3370, Issue4014` all moved\nto `[E0100] Cannot access field 'low'/'high'/'isInt64': class not registered`,\nlosing a PASS (conformance 431 -\u003e 430). Removing the dependency restored all six.\n\nThis is [[bugs-cross-module-new-dropped-by-compile-order]]'s family showing up\nfrom the stdlib side: order is load-bearing and an innocuous-looking import can\nsilently move it.\n\n**Prefer whatever the module already depends on.** `StringTools.hx` already used\n`StringBuf`, so reassembling code points through `StringBuf.addChar` cost nothing;\na byte buffer cost a PASS.\n\n**Method that made this cheap:** a 6-case mini-harness isolated it in ~3 minutes\ninstead of 40-minute battery runs —\n`SRC=\u003cdir-with-just-those-6-issues\u003e FEATURES=0 SUITES=unit OUT=/tmp/x.tsv ./run.sh`.\nThree arms (HEAD / full change / encoder-only) pinned the cause to one import.\nNote `Issue4675` flips CRASH \u003c-\u003e WRONG_ANSWER on an identical binary, so ignore\nit in any diff — see [[feature-isvar-backing-storage]] for the known flakes.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_untyped_deferred_local_reads_garbage` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}